Many of these spices you may already be familiar with. Some maybe not. For example, Thai cardamom (the white cardamom) is a common kind of cardamom used in Thai and Akha cooking rather than the green and the black cardamom, which can be replaced with one another.

Most of the spices used in Thailand are imported from overseas, like bay leaf, star anise seed, cinnamon, etc. Which makes it easy for you to get these spices in your supermarket. Maybe you already have them in your kitchen. Some can be rare and not familiar. For example Long pepper, Sichuan pepper, etc.

Quite often people asked. The recipe called for cumin seed to make a curry paste, I’ve got a powder. Can I use cumin powder? The answer is “Yes”. If you have powder then use the powder, if you got seed then use the seed. Doesn’t really matter, seed, pod, or powder, the result will be the same. This will go the same with all spices.

', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Flame', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 4, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('rice', 'ingredient', 'Rice', NULL, 'In Thailand, rice is primarily grown in ‘paddy fields’ – a flooded fields used for growing semi-aquatic crops. It is common for Thai families to have their own crops. Family members will share their rice crops with one another in order to create the best crop, which is then shared amongst the family.

The main types of rice in Thailand are white rice, brown rice, jasmine rice, and glutinous (sticky) rice. White rice is a staple component used to bulk meals and provides the main source of carbohydrates in the diet. Jasmine rice is used for sweet dishes such as mango sticky rice for its sweet and soft texture, where white rice is mainly used for savory dishes. Glutinous rice is different in texture – when you break the rice open it is creamy and soft inside. Similarly to white rice, brown rice is milled to remove to husk, however, it retains the bran layer.

Butterfly pea flower is a commonly used additive for coloring rice. To create a food coloring with butterfly pea flower, steep a dozen fresh or dried flowers in a cup of boiling water. After 15 minutes, strain the water and discard the flowers. You can now add this to your rice to create beautiful colors. Butterfly pea flowers can provide blue, pink, and purple colors. The color changes can be achieved by adding certain extra acidic ingredients, such as lime juice.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wheat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 1, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('meat', 'ingredient', 'Meats', NULL, 'The common meat that you are likely to find in Thailand is chicken or pork.

Due to the Hindu Buddhism country, beef is not commonly eaten in Thailand. Only a few restaurants serve beef. Southern parts of Thailand are more likely to eat beef than pork.

Seafood is common everywhere in Thailand, especially in the southern part of Thailand.
Freshwater fish is also another source of meat in Thailand, especially in the Northern and Eastern parts of Thailand like catfish, freshwater prawns, tilapia fish, frogs, etc.

Eggs and tofu are big supplements for protein needed from meat.

I love telling foreigners that. If you get 5-7 tiny pieces of pork, chicken, and shrimp in your order at a restaurant in Thailand. You got lucky. It’s your lucky day. The average there is in every dish is 4-5 tiny pieces of meat. Don’t be surprised if you order Shrimp Pad Thai. It comes out with 2-3 tiny shrimps. It is not a joke. They are not trying to cheat on you. It’s just the way it is. Thai food doesn’t cook or served with too much meat like western food. They add a few pieces just for flavor.

Most of the dishes in this cookbook can be made without meat or can be substituted with tofu. Or skip the meat if you would like to make it a vegan and vegetarian version.

', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Drumstick', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 5, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('herb', 'ingredient', 'Thai Herbs', NULL, 'There are lots of different kinds of herbs we use here in Thailand. Thai basil is similar to its European counterpart but its defining feature is its licorice-like taste. Galangal could be mistaken for ginger but has a subtler, more citrusy taste.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Leaf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 3, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('fruit', 'ingredient', 'Fruits', NULL, 'Maybe fruits are not common ingredients used in cooking in other cuisines. But in Thai and Akha cuisines many types of fruits are used as the main ingredients for cooking.

For example, papaya, you may think of yellow, ripe, sweet, and soft papaya fruit. But for cooking papaya has to be green papaya or unripe papaya fruit. The common dishes that you may already know are Papaya Salad, Keang Som Ma La Gor (Thai sour curry with green papaya), etc. Papaya can be used to create many different types of dishes from salads, soups, curries, and stir-fry dishes.

Jackfruit is also another example of using fruits for cooking. Young, immature fruit is used to make various dishes for vegan and vegetarian food. The texture and flavor of cooked Jackfruit are similar to pulled pork or chicken and full of nutrition.

In our recipes, there are a few fruits we mentioned but there are many kinds of fruits that can be used for cooking. Some may be easy to get in fresh, some may not but canned fruits also work well for cooking.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Apple', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 6, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('vegetable', 'ingredient', 'Fresh Vegetables', NULL, 'The best part of Thai and Akha food is using all fresh ingredients. There are various types of fresh vegetables used in Thai and Akha cooking. Some of them you may know already, and some of them you have never heard of before. Some may be available in dried or powder form.

For example turmeric, most people know turmeric powder and had used it before. For Thai and Akha cooking, they used fresh turmeric root then the turmeric powder. You may see these ingredients in Tom Yum Soup, they look like sliced baby carrots.

Regarding fresh ingredients, if you can’t get the particular ingredients. Don’t worry! In our recipes already mentioned the substitution for it. Like Thai eggplant to make Green Curry or Red Curry, if Thai eggplant is unavailable, you can use your regular purple eggplants or add broccoli or cauliflower to the curries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Carrot', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 2, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('misc', 'ingredient', 'Misc. Ingredients', NULL, 'There are many interesting miscellaneous ingredients that create perfect dishes and traditional Thai and Akha Food. Some may be easy to find and get at your supermarket, some may be difficult to get. Some you can eventually make your own from scratch. For example, Tom Yum Paste (Nam Prik Pao) makes Tom Yum Goong. You can get this paste from Asia Market or learn to make it from our cookbook.

A lot of these miscellaneous ingredients you are able to get at your supermarket or Asia market. Like fish sauce or soy sauce. It may not be the Thai chef’s favorite brand, but you can get Chinese or Vietnamese soy sauce or fish sauce which can be used to cook Thai Akha food.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Archive', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 7, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('appetizer', 'recipe', 'Appetizers', NULL, 'Foods that you might consider appetizers are viewed more as snacks in Thai culture. This would be something that we could eat at break time, when we''re in a rush or on the weekend when we''re hanging out with friends at a waterfall or in a park. For example, there''s nothing quite as satisfying as sitting down with friends to enjoy a beer and some papaya salad. Or when visiting the Sunday night market, we might pick up a spring roll for a snack while shopping. We call this type of food “Khong Gin Len”, which literally means “food to eat for fun”.', 'Start by preparing the famous Papaya Salad the authentic way using a mortar and pestle, followed by rolling the perfect fried spring rolls.', 'Can you take 5 chilies like the Thai?', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/showcase/bg-06.webp', 'UtensilsCrossed', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/song/GreenCurry.wav', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mention that Som Tum is traditionally very spicy, but students can customize the chilies.', '{"Use a wooden pestle for salads, stone for curry","Palm sugar must be dissolved completely"}', NULL, 0, '{}', true, 2, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-06 17:21:22.826101+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('rituals', 'history', 'Sacred Gates &', 'Ancestral beliefs and spiritual harmony', 'Learn about the spiritual village boundaries, the annual Women''s New Year, and the animist beliefs that maintain harmony.', NULL, NULL, 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/akha-history/01-spirit_gate.webp', 'Flame', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 3, '2026-04-03 14:55:25.56645+00', '2026-04-03 21:02:44.488738+00', NULL, NULL, 'Swing Festivals', 'Rituals'),
	('forest-to-table', 'history', 'From the Forest', 'Highland foraging and coffee revolution', 'Taste the tradition of sustainable highland farming, authentic recipes, and the modern evolution of the Akha coffee culture.', NULL, NULL, 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/akha-history/01-foragers_pantry.webp', 'Leaf', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '{}', true, 4, '2026-04-03 14:55:25.56645+00', '2026-04-03 21:02:44.488738+00', NULL, NULL, 'to the Table', 'Forest to Table'),
	('curry', 'recipe', 'Thai Curry & Paste', NULL, 'Thai curry is more watery and soupy than curries from other countries. In Thailand, local curries are not made from curry powder. Instead, we use chili paste. Some of the main ingredients in most curry pastes that you won''t find in many Western dishes include galangal, lemongrass, kaffir lime and shrimp paste. Thick Thai curries get their creaminess from coconut milk. Galangal (“khaa”) is a relative of the ginger plant, and it looks a bit similar. You may even hear it called “Thai ginger” in some cookbooks. But don''t confuse looks with taste for these two plants. Galangal tastes different than ginger, and its root (or rhizome) is very hard. Slicing it requires a sharp knife. Lemongrass is a long, grass-like plant with a fresh, lemony aroma and flavor. When cooking with lemongrass, trim the base and discard the outer layer. Reserve one-third of the white portion above the root for cooking. The kaffir lime (makrut) is a fruit with green skin that''s rough and bumpy. They''re relatively small – only 2 inches (5 cm) in width. In Thai cuisine, we use the kaffir lime leaves as well as the skin of the fruit for cooking. Coconut milk is made by combining water with coconut meat and blending them together. Coconut cream is very similar to coconut milk, but it contains less water. For this reason, coconut cream has a thicker, paste-like consistency than coconut milk.', 'Learn to make authentic curry paste from scratch using fresh ingredients, then choose and prepare one of the four most popular Thai curries [2, 3].', 'It’s Curry time! And we don’t mean the ready curry powders.', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/showcase/Recipes01.jpg', 'FlaskConical', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/song/GreenCurry.wav', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Highlight that we make paste from scratch. Explain the difference between Green (Fresh Chili) and Red (Dried Chili).', '{"Fry the paste until the oil separates","Bruise the lemongrass before chopping"}', NULL, 0, '{}', true, 4, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-06 17:21:22.826101+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('stirfry', 'recipe', 'Stir-Fried Dishes', NULL, 'Thai stir-fry is classic street food. Stir-fry always comes with rice on the side. In Thailand, we consider this to be fast food, because most restaurants are prepared to cook up a fast, single dish of this type of food and have it ready in minutes. Most stir-fries include vegetables and three or four pieces of chicken or pork. They''re intended to be eaten with rice. One of the stir-fry dishes we''re featuring here is Thai sweet and sour chicken. It''s not exactly the same as the Chinese version you may have tasted at home, but it does have strong Chinese influence. In fact, the most important flavoring ingredient in this dish is ketchup. Did you know that ketchup was originally invented in China? When English colonists were in Malaysia, they first tasted this Chinese condiment, and it soon became an international sensation. Today, ketchup is found basically everywhere in the world, and the same can probably be said for sweet and sour chicken. You''ll find that the Thai version is less sweet and syrupy than the international version. It uses pineapple for a citrusy kick and stir-fried (rather than deep-fried) chicken for an overall healthier effect. Stir-fried chicken with cashew nuts offers the fruity, nutty flavor of cashews along with a spicy kick from the sun-dried and roasted chilies. The cashew tree is large and evergreen, growing to 14 m (46 ft) tall. The true fruit of the cashew tree is a kidney-shaped or boxing-glove shaped fleshy fruit (or drupe) that grows at the end of the cashew apple. Even spicier still is the stir-fried chicken with hot basil, which uses fresh chilies and can be quite spicy if you prefer. It can also be toned down by using fewer chilies – or by leaving them out altogether. But the star of this dish is hot basil, which is a unique type of basil not often found overseas. But the most popular stir-fried dish in Thailand has to be pad Thai. In fact, it''s officially considered the national dish of Thailand. Ironically, pad Thai has Chinese origins. “Pad” is the Thai word for stir-fry, and Thai cooks created this dish by taking Chinese noodles (used in soups) and stir-frying them. This dish was made possible because of Chinese immigrants in Thailand, and today you''ll find street-food vendors selling pad Thai all over the country.', 'The grand finale [3]! Master classic Thai street food dishes in a wok, so you can easily impress your friends and family back home [3, 4].', 'The grand finale: classic Thai street food dishes.', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/showcase/Recipes01.jpg', 'Flame', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/song/GreenCurry.wav', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Emphasize speed and preparation (Mise en place). Mention Holy Basil vs Thai Basil.', '{"Prep everything before turning on the heat","The wok must be smoking hot"}', NULL, 0, '{}', true, 6, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-06 17:21:22.826101+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('soup', 'recipe', 'Thai Soups', NULL, 'The most popular way to eat Thai soup is with rice alongside a main course. You may also find yourself with friends at a local bar, drinking beer or whisky along with a spicy soup like “tom yum goong” (hot and sour soup with prawns). Enjoy a sip of beer, a sip of soup and continue. Thai people can go all night with a set-up like this! We call this type of food “gup gam”. My favorite Thai soup is coconut milk soup with chicken. It''s very creamy and full of the taste of coconut milk. This soup is called “tom kha gai”, which means boiled galangal with chicken. The galangal gives it a potent, ginger-like flavor. One of the most popular dishes for foreigners in Thailand is tom yum goong. In this case, “tom” means boiled again; “yum” refers to combination of spices that are sweet, spicy and sour; and “goong” refers to shrimp or prawns. It''s a delicious sweet, sour and spicy soup with prawns in it. I''ve also included a recipe for clear soup with egg tofu. You might compare this to the chicken noodle soup of Thailand. The flavors are mild, comforting and easy to eat. My mom used to make this soup for me for breakfast or when I was sick. And once I became an adult, I changed the name of this soup (at least in my mind) to “hangover soup”. It''s the perfect cure after a big night out!', 'Find out how Thai soup can taste so good [3]! Choose your favorite fragrant broth to prepare, with vegetarian substitutes always available [3].', 'Have you ever wondered how Thai soup can taste so good?', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/showcase/Recipes01.jpg', 'Soup', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/song/GreenCurry.wav', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Explain that soups are eaten with rice, not alone. Mention the health benefits of Galangal.', '{"Tear kaffir lime leaves to release oil","Do not boil coconut milk too vigorously or it separates"}', NULL, 0, '{}', true, 5, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-06 17:21:22.826101+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('akha_specialty', 'recipe', 'Traditional Akha Dishes', NULL, 'Akha dishes are not easy to find. You won''t find any recipes online because Akha people are an ethnic minority, and most people in the world don''t even know about them. But I was born and raised in an Akha village, and this is some of my favorite food on the planet. Akha food is totally different from Thai food, not to mention, much healthier and fresher. We use seasonal produce as a base for every meal. You could make a simple salad from the fresh ingredients, or you could steam, boil or stir-fry them for a hot dish. Every meal must be served with a spicy dipping sauce (“sapi thong”), one salad and one soup. Akha people have a playful saying about the types of ingredients we like to use: “There are only three things in the jungle that you can''t eat, and nobody knows what they are.” Akha saying In other words, we''ve scoured the jungle for things you can eat, and we haven''t found anything that''s not edible yet! We view ourselves as adventurous eaters. But for the purposes of this cookbook, I''ve focused on three of the most popular Akha dishes that you''re likely to find at a home in the village where I''m from. All of the dishes are made from mainstream ingredients, none of which are on that list of three things you cannot eat!', 'Discover a whole different world from Thai food [1, 2]. Master the traditional Akha trio: Chili Sauce, Mountain Fresh Salad, and Spirit Detox Soup [2].', 'A whole different world from Thai food.', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/showcase/Recipes01.jpg', 'Mountain', 'https://mtqullobcsypkqgdkaob.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/song/GreenCurry.wav', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'When discussing Akha Specialty, emphasize the Forest-to-Table philosophy and mention that Sapi Thong is eaten daily with fresh vegetables.', '{"Never use an electric blender for Sapi Thong","Roast the chilies over charcoal for smokiness"}', NULL, 0, '{}', true, 1, '2026-04-03 15:06:59.039972+00', '2026-04-06 17:21:22.826101+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);


